## 2 · Assertions presented as verified, not verified

These are claims the copies state as findings; no check in the tree supports them. Treat each as the agents' assertion.

| Copy | Assertion | Why it is not verified |
|---|---|---|
| module-audit | worker **FINISHED** | MET means code presence only; nothing was run, and there is no mutants record (V3 §5) |
| module-audit | PI-02 register admits any action | UNVERIFIABLE from the tree (V3 §1) |
| architecture-review | "task state written at ≥9 sites" | no site list in the file (V3 §5) |
| architecture-review | "21 inbound + 8 outbound hops, file:line for each" | no hop list in the file (E7) |
| DECISION_POINTS (v4) | EXACT 145 / THRESHOLD 42 | only JUDGMENT is recountable (E17) |
| interface-map | §9 host state (engine not running, release `38f3dfd2`, ollama pid 2508) | time-bound; not re-measured (V3 §5). The ATLAS M-1001 probe saw ollama MainPID 1899 |
| jev-decision-map | A4 (rate-limit change, 11 vs 9 jaggedness items) | an external page, unverifiable from the tree (V3 §5) |
